  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "{\"original_inventory_ordinal\":698,\"taxon\":\"Pachyornis elephantopus\",\"classification\":\"Dinornithiformes, Emeidae\",\"representation\":\"living-reconstruction\",\"reconstruction_type\":\"whole-organism\",\"scope\":\"Original low heavy moa body and exceptionally stout short lower legs; complete animal, subsequent pool not frozen72.\",\"scale\":{\"unit\":\"meter\",\"femur_m\":0.28,\"tibiotarsus_m\":0.445,\"tarsometatarsus_m\":0.223,\"measured_source\":\"Worthy and Holdaway1994 Ngarua Cave site3 specimen recovered by M.Endres, cranial voucherS27795. Not AM LB5950 or TePapaS.040230.\",\"resting_height_model_m\":1.15,\"height_status\":\"Estimated chosen neck posture, not a measured complete animal. NZBirdsOnline120cm is LENGTH, not shoulder or skull height.\",\"photo_scale\":\"TePapa S.040230 tarsometatarsus photo3cm bar; different specimen. Approx photographic bone length~0.22m supports proportions, not exact caliper measurement.\"},\"diagnostic_targets\":[\"Broad low heavy oval feathered trunk, no visible or vestigial wings.\",\"Exceptionally short stout tarsometatarsi and broad feet, unlike long slender ostrich legs.\",\"Long thick forward-curving neck, small rounded head and sturdy pointed decurved bill; no casque or giant duck bill.\",\"Three forward clawed toes plus small hind toe per foot, no ostrich two-toed feet or webbing.\",\"Restrained shaggy feather contour, scaly bare lower legs, no fan tail.\",\"Thighs covered by bulky body, readable negative spaces between stout legs and toes.\"],\"uncertainties\":[\"Living soft contour, posture and precise plumage pattern/colors are inferred; feather evidence permits variation, not a fixed proven painted pattern.\",\"AM LB5950 is mounted museum skeleton; mount pose and missing ribs do not define exact living silhouette.\",\"No claim that limb measurements, separate tarsometatarsus and skeleton photo are same individual.\",\"Tring photo caption says heavy-footed but filename says eastern-moa; it is excluded from production reference set to avoid ambiguous identity.\"]}",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：{\"original_inventory_ordinal\":698,\"taxon\":\"Pachyornis elephantopus\",\"classification\":\"Dinornithiformes, Emeidae\",\"representation\":\"living-reconstruction\",\"reconstruction_type\":\"whole-organism\",\"scope\":\"Original low heavy moa body and exceptionally stout short lower legs; complete animal, subsequent pool not frozen72.\",\"scale\":{\"unit\":\"meter\",\"femur_m\":0.28,\"tibiotarsus_m\":0.445,\"tarsometatarsus_m\":0.223,\"measured_source\":\"Worthy and Holdaway1994 Ngarua Cave site3 specimen recovered by M.Endres, cranial voucherS27795. Not AM LB5950 or TePapaS.040230.\",\"resting_height_model_m\":1.15,\"height_status\":\"Estimated chosen neck posture, not a measured complete animal. NZBirdsOnline120cm is LENGTH, not shoulder or skull height.\",\"photo_scale\":\"TePapa S.040230 tarsometatarsus photo3cm bar; different specimen. Approx photographic bone length~0.22m supports proportions, not exact caliper measurement.\"},\"diagnostic_targets\":[\"Broad low heavy oval feathered trunk, no visible or vestigial wings.\",\"Exceptionally short stout tarsometatarsi and broad feet, unlike long slender ostrich legs.\",\"Long thick forward-curving neck, small rounded head and sturdy pointed decurved bill; no casque or giant duck bill.\",\"Three forward clawed toes plus small hind toe per foot, no ostrich two-toed feet or webbing.\",\"Restrained shaggy feather contour, scaly bare lower legs, no fan tail.\",\"Thighs covered by bulky body, readable negative spaces between stout legs and toes.\"],\"uncertainties\":[\"Living soft contour, posture and precise plumage pattern/colors are inferred; feather evidence permits variation, not a fixed proven painted pattern.\",\"AM LB5950 is mounted museum skeleton; mount pose and missing ribs do not define exact living silhouette.\",\"No claim that limb measurements, separate tarsometatarsus and skeleton photo are same individual.\",\"Tring photo caption says heavy-footed but filename says eastern-moa; it is excluded from production reference set to avoid ambiguous identity.\"]}"
  },
